<title>UK: ICI shares fall after downgrade, chart break.</title>
<headline>ICI shares fall after downgrade, chart break.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc (ICI) fell on Tuesday as the stock slipped below a chart support level in the wake of a recent downgrade, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were 21p weaker at 710-1/2 by 1034 GMT. They broke below recent support at 730p, accelerating their fall, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Monday, analysts at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson downgraded the stock to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;, citing &quot;an underlying difficult trading environment&quot;.</p>
<p>Fellow chemicals firm BOC Group Plc also weakened, falling nine pence to 981-1/2.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Marshall, London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
